      "trigger": "A preparation CALL or pool CALL exhausts its forwarded gas while the executor retains enough gas under EIP-150 to report failure; all modes of that still-unproved direction then appear reverted while another direction succeeds.",
      "behavior": "BotVM opcode 0x00 observes only ok=false. _bubbleRuntimeHopFailure discards ordinary inner failure detail and reverts Error(\"call failed\"). The Rust strict backend records the outer ExecutionResult::Revert, and the TS transport converts a main Revert to CALL_EXCEPTION. Family decoding consequently treats that result as deterministic negative evidence and may publish only the other directions. In the old preCall path, a preparation OOG is an unresolved preCall/Halt. Injecting an already classified resource-limited result in the new tests does not cover this inner-to-outer conversion.",
      "impact": "A real resource-unknown direction can be omitted from an admitted pool rather than holding admission retryable. This is an admission/coverage correctness issue, not evidence of incorrect successful token balances or a demonstrated loss.",
